---
layout: layouts/base.njk
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <h1>{{ site.fullName }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{{ site.description }}</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved/">Get involved</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/knowledgebase/">Browse the knowledgebase</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <img class="hero-mark" src="/assets/img/fist-spray-paint.png" alt="ATP² raised-fist mark">
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Most tools for organizing get built by companies that need you to keep coming back, need your data to be worth something, or need a hierarchy somewhere in the stack. ATP² starts from a different assumption: <strong>the more distributed decision-making is, the more resilient the thing you're building becomes.</strong></p>
    <p>This site collects working knowledge — governance models, off-grid infrastructure, low-tech methods, and the tools that make coordinating without a boss easier — written to be used, argued with, and outgrown.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Recently added</h2>
  </div>
  <ul class="entry-list">
    {% for item in collections.recent %}
    <li class="entry">
      <h3 class="entry-title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h3>
      <p class="entry-meta">
        <time datetime="{{ item.date | dateISO }}">{{ item.date | dateReadable }}</time>
        {% for tag in item.data.tags %}{% if tag != "knowledgebase" and tag != "articles" %}<span class="tag">{{ tag }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </p>
      {% if item.data.summary %}<p class="entry-summary">{{ item.data.summary }}</p>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
